      "text": [
        "324 - وَقَالَ أَبُو اَلْحَسَنِ مُوسَى بْنُ جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «ثَلاَثٌ مَنْ عَرَفَهُنَّ لَمْ يَدَعْهُنَّ جَزُّ اَلشَّعْرِ وَ تَشْمِيرُ اَلثَّوْبِ وَ نِكَاحُ اَلْإِمَاءِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.324 - Abu al-Hasan Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as) said:\n\"There are three things which, if a person understands them, they will not abandon: trimming the hair, shortening the garment, and marrying bondwomen.\""
        ]
      }
